  "id": "sudden-insight",
  "term": "sudden insight",
  "definition": "Sudden insight is the experience in problem solving of a solution coming to mind all at once and seeming obviously right. In this context, stronger feelings of insight are more often reported for correct solutions than for incorrect ones, especially on problems meant to evoke insight.",
